  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Defenders Partnership (DDP) 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Digital Defenders Partnership (DDP) 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det krympande demokratiska utrymmet begr&#xe4;nsar verksamhetsytorna f&#xf6;r akt&#xf6;rer som verkar f&#xf6;r demokrati, m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och yttrandefrihet globalt. F&#xf6;rf&#xf6;ljelse, &#xf6;vervakning och censur genom digitala kanaler &#xf6;kar och utvecklas successivt. F&#xf6;rtryckande regeringar censurerar information av allm&#xe4;nt intresse, utvidgar &#xf6;vervakningen och sin kunskap om hur de kan &#xf6;ka sin kontroll &#xf6;ver den digitala arenan. De digitala systemens s&#xe5;rbarhet och deras m&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r &#xf6;vervakning anv&#xe4;nds f&#xf6;r att identifiera och kontrollera journalister, bloggare, aktivister och MR-f&#xf6;rsvarare.  F&#xf6;r att skydda dessa viktiga internetanv&#xe4;ndare och f&#xf6;r att h&#xe5;lla internet &#xf6;ppet och gratis, bildades Digital Defenders Partnership (DDP) 2012 av Freedom Online Coalition (FOC) - ett partnerskap mellan 31 regeringar som har &#xe5;tagit sig att arbeta tillsammans f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja internetfrihet och skydda grundl&#xe4;ggande m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter - fritt uttryck, f&#xf6;rening- och m&#xf6;tesfrihet och s&#xe4;kerhet online - &#xf6;ver hela v&#xe4;rlden. Sverige &#xe4;r en av medlemmarna i FOC.

Hivos har inkommit med ett programf&#xf6;rslag till Sida om fortsatt finansiering av Digital Defenders Partnership basketfond under fyra &#xe5;r (2020-2023) med 28 MSEK, vilket &#xe4;r cirka 14% av den planerade budgeten. Genom att ge r&#xe5;d och ekonomiskt st&#xf6;d (akutrespons) till individer, syftar Digital Defenders Partnership att &#xf6;ka den digitala och fysiska s&#xe4;kerhet f&#xf6;r journalister, bloggare, aktivister och MR-f&#xf6;rsvarare. Vidare kommer DDP att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten av lokala, regionala och globala n&#xe4;tverk f&#xf6;r att snabbt kunna agera n&#xe4;r individer och eller organisationer i deras n&#xe4;tverk uts&#xe4;tts f&#xf6;r hot eller attacker. DDP kommer &#xe4;ven att bidra till l&#xe5;ngsiktigt st&#xe4;rkande av organisationers digitala s&#xe4;kerhet f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka deras resiliens mot attacker och &#xf6;vervakning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internet freedom is under threat worldwide. Repressive governments across the world censor information of public interest, expand surveillance and crack down on privacy tools. Critical internet users such as bloggers, cyber-activists, journalists and human rights defenders are challenged in repressive environments. They face targeted hacking and attacks as well as surveillance and censorship threats. To protect these critical internet users and to keep the internet open and free, the Digital Defenders Partnership (DDP) was established in 2012 by the Freedom Online Coalition (FOC) - a partnership of 31 governments who have committed to work together to support Internet freedom and protect fundamental human rights &#x2013; free expression, association, assembly, and privacy online &#x2013; worldwide. Sweden is one of the governments in FOC.

Hivos has submitted a programme proposal for continued funding of theDigital Defenders Partnership basket fund for four years (2020-2023) with 28 MSEK, which is about 14% of the projected budget. By providing advice and financial support to individuals, Digital Defenders Partnership aims to increase digital and physical safety for Human Rights Defenders (HRD) under attack. In addition, DDP also aims to increase the capacity of the digital emergency response eco-system, referring to the combination of all the different players in this integrated mechanism of response. It does so by investing in key responders who provide services to critical internet users. Through that DDP aims to further develop structural emergency response capacity, in order to provide rapid responses in case of digital emergencies in repressive internet environments.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Digital Defenders Partnership&apos;s overall objective for the coming strategic period is that Human Rights Defenders(HRDs) remain resilient to closing civic space and continue to effectively use the internet and information and communications technology to promote and defend human rights.
DDP has formulated three strategic goals that contribute towards acheving the overall objective:
1. Provide timely, flexible and holistic emergency response resources to reduce the impactor risk of digital attacks against human rights defenders;
2. Strengthen awareness and capacities for sustainable and effective responses to digital threats among human rights defenders at risk;
3. Develop, maintain, and support accessible, collaborative, resilient and responsive networks of expertise and support for human rights defenders under digital threat.</narrative>
  </description>
